                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "08a4091e-5977-4d50-ad59-5118d9ca0f77",
                        "entry_id": "aca36e2b-6f29-31c2-88f4-2bbeac7c236c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "pachons"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9966b64b-ef5c-3091-86a3-f021230adbb7",
                        "entry_id": "aca36e2b-6f29-31c2-88f4-2bbeac7c236c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Piquet de bois auquel on attache les vaches dans les alpages."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bbaa7eaf-54f2-41f3-bbe3-af807de77c12",
                                "sense_id": "9966b64b-ef5c-3091-86a3-f021230adbb7",
                                "text": "Car les bêtes passent la nuit attachées chacune à un piquet qu'on appelle un pachon."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e8d64fc3-0a26-4dc4-9c3d-3de98bb14fdf",
                                "sense_id": "9966b64b-ef5c-3091-86a3-f021230adbb7",
                                "text": "Ayant attaché l'animal par une corde de chanvre à un pachon, il fait consciencieusement la traite, assis sur un tabouret à un seul pied, la « salla du pachon », qui se fiche en terre."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "712a5388-aa17-3815-af4c-f789d8432c18",
                        "entry_id": "aca36e2b-6f29-31c2-88f4-2bbeac7c236c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Bâton en bois qu’utilise parfois le télémarkeur pour s’équilibrer."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "378c84f6-1be8-410f-b4ee-96e28a4432be",
                                "sense_id": "712a5388-aa17-3815-af4c-f789d8432c18",
                                "text": "Les moniteurs, entre eux, nomment « pachons » les piquets qui servent au traçage des slaloms . Le pachon est le piquet auquel on attachait les vaches pour fumer les alpages."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3aa27f68-83f9-4648-ba18-1d43ee385548",
                        "source_entry_id": "aca36e2b-6f29-31c2-88f4-2bbeac7c236c",
                        "target_lang_word": "lurk",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lurk",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "20469fef-0daa-3f54-b838-ffacc2f24459",
                                        "entry_id": "7e29215d-c9c6-3889-be68-09b4f88330d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To remain concealed in order to ambush."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "add9c97d-0489-438b-8113-6385ff816143",
                                                "sense_id": "20469fef-0daa-3f54-b838-ffacc2f24459",
                                                "text": "Even without hovering drones, a lurking assassin, a thumping score and a denouement, the real-life story of Edward Snowden, a rogue spy on the run, could be straight out of the cinema. But, as with Hollywood, the subplots and exotic locations may distract from the real message: America’s discomfort and its foes’ glee."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a4379cc-d355-44ad-95f0-e4fa1d78e809",
                                                "sense_id": "20469fef-0daa-3f54-b838-ffacc2f24459",
                                                "text": "Things lurking in the dark / They like to leave a mark / Inside of you"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5419108b-003e-3f11-98a6-9800d94a0be5",
                                        "entry_id": "7e29215d-c9c6-3889-be68-09b4f88330d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To remain unobserved."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "39d3f323-bd9b-4932-913d-70f38ec8d4d5",
                                                "sense_id": "5419108b-003e-3f11-98a6-9800d94a0be5",
                                                "text": "Thus my plight was evil indeed, for I had nothing now to burn to give me light, and knew that 'twas no use setting to grout till I could see to go about it. Moreover, the darkness was of that black kind that is never found beneath the open sky, no, not even on the darkest night, but lurks in close and covered places and strains the eyes in trying to see into it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4fcd300f-83d3-38bd-a132-be2854760915",
                                        "entry_id": "7e29215d-c9c6-3889-be68-09b4f88330d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To hang out or wait around a location, preferably without drawing attention to oneself."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b52d97c-6f84-4bc2-950a-b341a736281c",
                                                "sense_id": "4fcd300f-83d3-38bd-a132-be2854760915",
                                                "text": "if we find the sophist lurking, we must round him up by royal command of the argument"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e6cf9751-2c27-3a97-ad9b-d517b22f9025",
                                        "entry_id": "7e29215d-c9c6-3889-be68-09b4f88330d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To read an Internet forum without posting comments or making one's presence apparent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Internet"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8f0c6bb7-7c5c-35cf-8019-ff56c7b58a22",
                                        "entry_id": "7e29215d-c9c6-3889-be68-09b4f88330d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To saddle (a person) with an undesirable task or duty."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "slang",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e4829fb-e036-47a1-8842-8dfc8bc23408",
                                                "sense_id": "8f0c6bb7-7c5c-35cf-8019-ff56c7b58a22",
                                                "text": "As junior dogsbody, he was lurked with this mission."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "lurk",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "181e0cf4-b264-35d7-b667-be838bc10a8d",
                                        "entry_id": "851c4567-da82-3fe3-96f0-5429a061b42f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of lurking."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d4fffe45-32a4-4cfb-a377-09f7ff1497c9",
                                                "sense_id": "181e0cf4-b264-35d7-b667-be838bc10a8d",
                                                "text": "At two p.m. a man had called on him, and had produced one of his advertisements, and had asked him if that was all square—no bobbies on the lurk."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df8487bf-6231-4064-95e1-cd27d15a16ff",
                                                "sense_id": "181e0cf4-b264-35d7-b667-be838bc10a8d",
                                                "text": "There were enemies on the lurk and time was against him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d91a6bb0-207e-45a4-9eba-e6de89479f4e",
                                                "sense_id": "181e0cf4-b264-35d7-b667-be838bc10a8d",
                                                "text": "[…] barked furiously and made at him as at a wolf, and before he could wholly rise from the lurk because of the sudden consternation, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa6fe27a-9384-3764-97b8-56e0f69f0b48",
                                        "entry_id": "851c4567-da82-3fe3-96f0-5429a061b42f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A swindle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Australia",
                                            "UK",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
